{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-volume","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:quantum-volume","kind":"definition","title":"Quantum volume","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-reeb-bundle"],"tags":["volume","statistical-mechanics","categorical-volume","s3-fibre","reeb-bundle"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.quantumVolume","text":"quantum-volume.md","leanSource":"quantum-volume.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:quantum-volume\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S} \\to M</code> be the state bundle with Reeb bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S^3 \\to \\mathcal{S}_p</code> at each brane point <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>. The <strong>quantum volume</strong> of a region <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U \\subset M</code> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  V_q(U) = \\int_U \\mathrm{Vol}_{S^3}(\\mathcal{S}_p)\\; \\epsilon_q(p),</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\epsilon_q</code> is the categorical volume form on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda^2 V</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-volume.md","heading":"Definition","number":"22.9.9","page":"b/def-quantum-volume","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Information.quantumVolume","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-volume.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
